// movecheck's half of the boundary, and the reason this defect lived
// only in codegen. #459 established "is this expression a value?" as a
// movecheck question and rejected `void` wherever a value is required --
// but deliberately asked it only of the conditional's *condition*, not
// of its arms, on the grounds that [basic.types.general] permits a
// `void` second and third operand and the result is then a `void`
// expression like any other: legal if discarded, caught by whichever
// position tries to bind it (see the movetest cases next to this one).
//
// So this already passed movecheck before the fix and still does. It is
// here to pin that decision down: if a later change makes movecheck
// reject a discarded `void` conditional, that is a regression against
// #459's model, and codegen accepting it would no longer be reachable
// to notice.
int taken = 0;

void h() { taken = 1; }
void h2() { taken = 2; }

int main() {
    bool c = true;
    c ? h() : h2();
    return 0;
}
